{"xson":[{"/iati-activities/iati-activity":[{"/activity-date":[{"@iso-date":"2011-12-13","@type":"2"},{"@iso-date":"2018-09-30","@type":"4"}],"/activity-status@code":"4","/collaboration-type@code":"2","/contact-info":[{"/department/narrative":[{"1":"MCO-EGY","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/email":[{"1":"t.al-eryani@ifad.org"}],"/job-title/narrative":[{"1":"Country Director","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/organisation/narrative":[{"1":"International Fund for Agricultural Development","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/person-name/narrative":[{"1":"Al-Eryani, Thoodan Abdulkarim Ali","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/telephone":[{"1":"+390654591"}],"/website":[{"1":"http://www.ifad.org"}],"@type":"1"}],"/default-aid-type":[{"@code":"C01","@vocabulary":"1"}],"/default-tied-status@code":"5","/description":[{"/narrative":[{"1":"The project's overall goal is to improve the food security, incomes and resilience to shocks of smallholder producers (including young people and women) in rainfed areas of North Kordofan and South Kordofan. Its development objective is to increase crop productivity for about 108,000 smallholder producers adopting certified seeds in North Kordofan and South Kordofan.The project has four components that are complementary and mutually reinforcing. The primary focus of the first component is on the regulatory environment and institutional strengthening for the public sector. The second component provides the necessary support for enhancing the performance of the seed production system. The third component is designed to support the development of the seed market, and includes support to farmers' groups and associations and facilitation of their timely access to certified seeds. The fourth component provides for the coordination of the project.","@xml:lang":"EN"}]}],"/document-link":[{"/category":[{"@code":"A12"}],"/description/narrative":[{"1":"More information on how IFAD publish IATI data to ensure the effectiveness of development.","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/language":[{"@code":"EN"}],"/title/narrativ